# Behavioral Experiments in Health Economics

**Authors:** Matteo M. Galizzi, Daniel Wiesen

## Abstract
<p>The state-of-the-art literature at the interface between experimental and behavioral economics and health economics is reviewed by identifying and discussing 10 areas of potential debate about behavioral experiments in health. By doing so, the different streams and areas of application of the growing field of behavioral experiments in health are reviewed, by discussing which significant questions remain to be discussed, and by highlighting the rationale and the scope for the further development of behavioral experiments in health in the years to come.</p>

**Source:** https://doi.org/10.1093/acrefore/9780190625979.013.244

